  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the largest government contractors by contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Total federal contract obligations reported on the page equal $235B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. leads the list with $19.9B in obligations, followed by TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $14.5B and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO with $13.4B. The list includes large defense and nondefense vendors: LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice with $12.5B and $10.6B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is at $10.8B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY is at $8.2B. THE BOEING COMPANY and BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED each appear with $5.9B. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals, not full fiscal year results.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who tops the FY2026 to date list?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. tops the list with $19.9B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO follow with $14.5B and $13.4B respectively. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears on the list twice with $12.5B and $10.6B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How many contractors are included in the top ranking?",
        "body": "The top ranking lists ten contractor entries. The entries include a mix of commercial services, construction, and defense suppliers by name and obligation amount. Total obligations across the report equal $235B."
